                </head>

                <body style="margin:0; padding:0; background:#f4f4f4;">

                        <!-- PREHEADER (hidden, controls inbox preview snippet) -->
                        <div
                                style="display:none; max-height:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; color:#f4f4f4; opacity:0;">
                                Modon.com
                                &nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;
                        </div>

                        <!-- CENTER WRAPPER: <center> is the most reliable way to force
                             centering in Outlook's Word rendering engine, which ignores
                             CSS text-align/margin:auto on tables -->
                        <center style="width:100%; background:#f4f4f4;">

                        <!--[if mso]>
                        <table role="presentation" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="600" style="width:600px;">
                        <tr>
                        <td>
                        <![endif]-->

                                                <!-- CONTENT TABLE -->
                                                <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                                                        border="0" align="center"
                                                        style="width:600px; max-width:600px; margin:0 auto; background:#ffffff; border-collapse:collapse; mso-table-lspace:0pt; mso-table-rspace:0pt;">

                                                        <!-- HEADER -->
                                                        <tr>
                                                                <td style="padding:0; line-height:0; font-size:0;">
                                                                        <img src="https://image.realestate.modon.com/lib/fe2e117373640475741678/m/1/b1abaafe-d719-4fc6-833b-aec29cfb602c.jpg"
                                                                                alt="Modon Header" width="600"
                                                                                
                                                                                style="display:block; width:600px; height:auto; border:0; outline:none; text-decoration:none;" />
                                                                </td>
                                                        </tr>

                                                        <!-- BODY -->
                                                        <tr>
                                                                <td
                                                                        style="padding:14px 32px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; color:#000000;">
                                                                        <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Dear
                                                                                <b> Francisco Galan / Mohammed Abdelrazik,</b></p>

                                                                        
    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">	We would like to bring to your attention the PDCs related to <b>{!SalesOrder__c.Name}</b>, created on <b> {!SalesOrder__c.SOCreationDate__c}</b> for <b>{!SalesOrder__c.CustomerAccount__c}</b>.</p>

                                                                        <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
Despite multiple reminders and successive escalations to the assigned salesperson and Sales Director, the required PDCs have not yet been received. To date, no satisfactory resolution or confirmed timeline for collection has been provided.                                         </p>

                                                                        <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;">
                   The continued absence of these PDCs places the order outside the agreed payment terms and exposes the business to potential cancellations risks. All previous escalation channels have been exhausted without resolution.
                                                                        </p>
                                                                        
   <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;">
We would appreciate your guidance and support in resolving this matter urgently and request confirmation of the next steps, along with an expected timeline for the collection and submission of the outstanding PDCs.
                                                                        </p>

                                                                </td>
                                                        </tr>

                                                        <tr>
                                                                <td
                                                                        style="padding:14px 32px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; color:#000000;">
                                                               
                                                                        </p>

                                                                        <p style="margin:0;">Thank You,</p>
                                                                        <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Modon</strong></p>
                                                                </td>
                                                        </tr>

                                                        <!-- FOOTER -->
                                                        <tr>
                                                                <td bgcolor="#000000" style="padding:0px 0px;">
